My first real illiterate ascension after losing illiterate and wishless
last month in a stupid Bell of Opening accident.  Lost polyitem while
IDing potions by dipping.   

The only remarkable thing about this game was the number of artifacts I
acquired without really trying.  Sacrificing got me Cleaver first (of
course).  Accidental crowning got me Vorpy.  However, Magicbane and
Frostbrand were found just sort of laying around and Sunsword was on an
early angelic.  A balrog had Ogresmasher for some reason.  

Used Cleaver until I found Frosty, then switched out so I could wear a
SoR and "oESP instead of an "oR.  Switched to Vorpy permanently after
crowning.  Without the ability to enchant, the difference in damage was
fairly trivial, and Vorpy is terrific against covetous monsters.  

MR came from a CoMR I got off the only bones file of any use.  Wore some
terrifically unenchanted armor for most of the game, having found plenty
of gear in the mines.  Early GoP were essentially useless, since the
tiny increase in carrying capacity couldn't overcome the lack of BoH for
nearly the whole game (finally found one in Orcus town.  Good enough).  

Ludios was a godsend, providing me with a bit of +4 and +5 armor.
Stashed the highest enchanted stuff so I could pick it up on the run to
the planes and wore the second-best choices on my way down.  9 points of
protection plus 10 points or so of enchantment plus dwarvish mithril
gave me an AC of about -20 going into gehennom.  With stealth, /oTele,
=oConflict, and alchemy, it wasn't bad at all.  

A bit of mindflayer trouble going down, but otherwise uneventful.  Used
a couple of /oDeath charges on Rodney and cleared out the Sanctum with
conflict.  Had a great run with Vorpy, beheading three fooliches in a
row.  :) 

Not so much luck on the way up, getting swarmed with nasties many times
and having my unihorn hit with two curses in quick succession, leading
to some stupid self-confusion.  For the first time, I had to actually
dig down to escape on the way up with the AoY.  :(  Should have used
?oScareMonster.  

The Planes were a pain, having no way to locate the portals.  Put on the
AoY and went searching.  Earth took longer than it should have, as the
amulet seemed reluctant to help.  Air wasn't bad.  /oPoly took out the
elementals and I eventually wandered into the portal.  Waited around for
a while on Fire until a bunch of the traps were mapped out, then set
off, staying over lava as much as possible.  An Archon showed up, but I
got lucky and Vorpy took him out in one hit.  Eventually, a fire vortex
wandered onto the portal.  Water was a pain.  I had saved my /oSDD for
this, but it still took forever.  Got sick of waiting and put on my
=oLev.  Ended up wandering into the portal without a single warning from
the amulet.  

Astral was fairly uneventful.  Went in without conflict and set out for
Famine.  He never got a chance to touch me, between the death rays and
getting beaten to death by angels.  The altar was Chaotic, so I whipped
out the HoOA.  Unfortunately, switching helms took me up to AC:-6 and
very vulnerable.  Lawful.  Lawful.  Lawful.  Lawful.  I thought I was
doing something wrong.  Had to quaff a !oFH at one point, but never put
on the "oLS.  Eventually, it worked out.  Chaotic.  #offer.  

